  "grid": "every layer strip is 64x22 on the same grid as the full strips (no offsets); alpha 0/255; draw in \"order\" with plain alpha-over",
  "outlineRule": "each layer carries its own K outline, except where it touches the body+cloak silhouette (the body/cloak outline already covers that)",
  "body": "legs, face, hair, jerkin, tunic and the K outline that touches them (holes where the cloak goes: always draw a cloak layer; there is no \"no cloak\" walker)",
  "cloak": "hood + cloak placeholders mapped per variant (green G/n, fur O/D/C, oilskin S/K/s) + the variant extras",
  "hood": "head-slot hood colours: recolour only the hood pixels (rows 0-8 of the body art) and are drawn over the cloak",
  "armour": "recolours the jerkin (padded O/C, mail s/S checker + mail skirt, plate s/S/w + steel skirt); the belt stays on top",
  "lantern": "\"<v>\" = rear hand (sword/spear/axe/mace); \"<v>-belt\" = hung at the rear hip. Use -belt with bow, crossbow and any shield (same rule as the 16-bit sheets)",
  "shield": "on the rear arm, x 0-4 (buckler O/D wood, kite R/E paint like the P1 shields); fist T at x 4",
  "trinket": "harefoot: O cap + C fur at x 11, rows 15-17 (front of the belt)",
  "check": "walkers_export.py rebuilt 5400 combinations (3 cloaks x 5 helmets x 6 weapons x 3 qualities x shields/none x armour x hood) from the saved layer PNGs and compared them with the direct strips: 0 mismatches"
 },
